From 0754f88cf31bc485a333169e3b3f0a56604e5172 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:33:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(finish3d): land model - fill closed openings on the
 drive surface

A 3D Finish option, `fill_openings` (mm, off by default), plans the path
on the model plus horizontal lids over every closed hole or pocket a flat
disk of that diameter cannot enter (grey-scale morphological closing of
the top-down height field; openings that run out to an edge or would
spill over a lower rim are never filled). The finish flies over bolt
holes at their rim instead of diving down their walls, and the path
says what stands as land. Lids are only ever added, so the path can
rise, never sink; the verifier still judges the real model. Undoable op
param, carried by the MCP params door, UI field on the 3D Finish page;
Geodesic refuses the combination by name. Off is byte-identical (no
digest bytes, no file key).

Fixes #1196

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
